        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: زمن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زمن — zaman — \"an age, a span of time\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كان ذلك في زمن جدي. kāna dhālika fī zaman jaddī. That was in my grandfather’s time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: أزمنة, azmina."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وقت is a time for something; زمن (zaman) is time as a stretch, an age."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زمن (zaman) is built on the native Arabic root z-m-n (Lane), where zaman and zamān name time, a short span or a long one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
