          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عهد — ʿahd — \"a reign, an era; a pledge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بني الجسر في عهد الملك الأول. buniya al-jisr fī ʿahd al-malik al-awwal. The bridge was built in the reign of the first king."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: عهود, ʿuhūd."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في عهد (ʿahd): in the days of, under. Also a promise: وفى بالعهد, he kept the pledge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عهد (ʿahd) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-h-d (Lane), \"to enjoin, to bind by a compact\". A ruler's pledge marks his time, so ʿahd is also a reign."
            }
          ]
        },
